      "text": "Prosody is the formal study of poetic meter, rhythm, and sound. Poetry is language organized by formal constraints on sound — constraints that may be quantitative (duration), accentual (stress), syllabic (count), or tonal (pitch). Different languages use different prosodic systems because their phonological structure differs."
    },
