      },
      "text": "COMMON VARIATIONS IN IAMBIC PENTAMETER:\nTrochaic inversion at line start: common and natural\n  \"TIGER, tiger, burning bright\" — trochee opening\nFeminine ending: unstressed extra syllable at end\n  \"To BE or NOT to BE, that IS the QUES-tion\" (11 syllables)\nCaesura: mid-line pause (marked |)\n  \"Shall I compare thee | to a summer's day\"\nEnjambment: line runs on without pause to next line\n  (opposite of end-stopped)\n```"
    },
