        "id": "maxim:literature:poetry-forms",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "literature",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[poetry, forms]",
        "section": "literature",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Poetry Forms and Prosody",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The pattern is a specific mathematical permutation:\n  Each stanza rotates the previous by the rule:\n  last → first, then alternate from outside in.\n  This is sometimes called \"retrogradatio cruciata\"\n  (reverse cruciform movement)."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-POETRY-FORMS.md#031",
      "path": [
        "05-POETRY-FORMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:literature:05-poetry-forms, git-history:literature:05-poetry-forms]",
        "canonical_path": "literature/05-POETRY-FORMS.md",
        "concepts": "[poetry, forms]",
        "current_path": "literature/05-POETRY-FORMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:literature:poetry-forms",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "literature",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[poetry, forms]",
        "section": "literature",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Poetry Forms and Prosody",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The effect: by the final stanza, every possible\nrelationship between the 6 words has been expressed.\nThe end-words themselves become the poem's subject —\nthey accrete meaning through each new context.\n```"
    },
