      "text": "```\nPINDARIC ODE — TRIADIC STRUCTURE"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-POETRY-FORMS.md#037",
      "path": [
        "05-POETRY-FORMS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:literature:05-poetry-forms, git-history:literature:05-poetry-forms]",
        "canonical_path": "literature/05-POETRY-FORMS.md",
        "concepts": "[poetry, forms]",
        "current_path": "literature/05-POETRY-FORMS.md",
        "id": "maxim:literature:poetry-forms",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "literature",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[poetry, forms]",
        "section": "literature",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Poetry Forms and Prosody",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Each TRIAD:\n  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n  │ STROPHE      (στροφή = \"turn\")                              │\n  │  Meter:  [x / u / u u / u u / u / ...]   [Pindar's own      │\n  │          complex lyric meters; no English equivalent]       │\n  │  Chorus physically turns left across the orchestra          │\n  │  Content: opens the myth or narrative                       │\n  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ ANTISTROPHE  (ἀντιστροφή = \"counter-turn\")                  │\n  │  Meter:  IDENTICAL to strophe                               │\n  │  Chorus turns right (reversing the strophe's movement)      │\n  │  Content: continues/develops the myth                       │\n  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n  │ EPODE        (ἐπῳδός = \"after-song\")                        │\n  │  Meter:  DIFFERENT from strophe/antistrophe (shorter)       │\n  │  Chorus stands still                                        │\n  │  Content: concludes the mythic passage; applies to athlete  │\n  └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n  Repeated: 3–5 triads per ode."
    },
